  "result": "Fixed. Shell completion now treats `#` as an ordinary character instead of the start of a comment.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment start by default. Everything from a `#` onward was silently dropped from the completion words.\n\n**Fix:** set `lex.commenters = \"\"` on the lexer.\n\n**Test:** added `test_split_arg_string_hash_not_comment` in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`. All 59 tests in that file pass.\n\nI didn't add a changelog entry, since the top section (8.5.0) is already released.",
